{"type":"message","id":"27097faa","parentId":"3cd528f5","timestamp":"2026-03-25T14:16:41.481Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"web_search_1774448200080_655","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"openclaw check cron jobs documentation\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1334,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdb71c038b53308f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCron Jobs - OpenClaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdb71c038b53308f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://docs.openclaw.ai/automation/cron-jobs\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b335b0fa524b71d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor cron schedules: <strong>confirm timezone (--tz) vs the host timezone</strong>. OpenClaw applies exponential retry backoff for recurring jobs after consecutive errors: 30s, 1m, 5m, 15m, then 60m between retries.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b335b0fa524b71d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"docs.openclaw.ai\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ead4435048f56fd7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw Cron Jobs: 8 Automation Templates, Schedules, and Debug Steps | Stack Junkie\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ead4435048f56fd7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.stack-junkie.com/blog/openclaw-cron-jobs-automation-guide\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c48f44dc2cd637b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Use openclaw cron list to find the job ID</strong>. Disabled jobs show Enabled: false in the list. ... # Check scheduler status openclaw cron status # Run a job immediately (for testing) openclaw cron run &lt;jobId&gt; # View run history for a job openclaw ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2c48f44dc2cd637b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 13, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.stack-junkie.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88eac429a0811352\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCron Jobs – OpenClaw - Open Source AI Coding Assistant\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88eac429a0811352\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclawlab.com/en/docs/automation/cron-jobs/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0f91ee639faac77c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCheck the Gateway is running continuously (cron runs inside the Gateway process). For cron schedules: <strong>confirm timezone (--tz) vs the host timezone</strong>. OpenClaw applies exponential retry backoff for recurring jobs after consecutive errors: 30s, 1m, 5m, 15m, then 60m between retries.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0f91ee639faac77c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"2 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openclawlab.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22689147cb371693\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nr/AI_Agents on Reddit: What's the recommended way to set up cron jobs for OpenClaw?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22689147cb371693\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/AI_Agents/comments/1quqd5m/whats_the_recommended_way_to_set_up_cron_jobs_for/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"23307019c40a2740\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHere&#x27;s a site with a listing of cron jobs you can run with the command to put into the terminal window. Contribute if you have any good ones creativecron.ai ... Hi, I was talking about buying the Fun60 pro keyboard. It looks great, but since I work with Adobe, I&#x27;d like to know how to set up the arrow keys. Any advice? ... [OpenClaw] Cron jobs &amp; background tasks execute but fail to send Telegram messages (silent failures)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"23307019c40a2740\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 3, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.reddit.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a65ff32d1fb89d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Complete OpenClaw Architecture That Actually Scales — Memory, Cron Jobs, Dashboard, and the…\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a65ff32d1fb89d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://medium.com/@rentierdigital/the-complete-openclaw-architecture-that-actually-scales-memory-cron-jobs-dashboard-and-the-c96e00ab3f35\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1a9fea92776788fa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe patterns below (memory, cron, dashboard, skills) haven’t changed — but the model layer did. What’s different now: My stack runs Kimi K2.5 primary + MiniMax M2.5 fallback, via OpenRouter on two $5/month VPS (Hostinger + Hetzner). $200/month → $15. The architecture got simpler — no OAuth management, no rate limit dancing. Full migration: rebuilt for $15. I’ve been running OpenClaw daily since it was still called Clawdbot.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1a9fea92776788fa\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"1 week ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"medium.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"openclaw check cron jobs documentation","provider":"brave","count":5,"tookMs":1334,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"brave","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bdb71c038b53308f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCron Jobs - OpenClaw\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bdb71c038b53308f\">>>","url":"https://docs.openclaw.ai/automation/cron-jobs","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4b335b0fa524b71d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFor cron schedules: <strong>confirm timezone (--tz) vs the host timezone</strong>. OpenClaw applies exponential retry backoff for recurring jobs after consecutive errors: 30s, 1m, 5m, 15m, then 60m between retries.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4b335b0fa524b71d\">>>","siteName":"docs.openclaw.ai"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ead4435048f56fd7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOpenClaw Cron Jobs: 8 Automation Templates, Schedules, and Debug Steps | Stack Junkie\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ead4435048f56fd7\">>>","url":"https://www.stack-junkie.com/blog/openclaw-cron-jobs-automation-guide","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2c48f44dc2cd637b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>Use openclaw cron list to find the job ID</strong>. Disabled jobs show Enabled: false in the list. ... # Check scheduler status openclaw cron status # Run a job immediately (for testing) openclaw cron run &lt;jobId&gt; # View run history for a job openclaw ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2c48f44dc2cd637b\">>>","published":"February 13, 2026","siteName":"www.stack-junkie.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"88eac429a0811352\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCron Jobs – OpenClaw - Open Source AI Coding Assistant\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"88eac429a0811352\">>>","url":"https://openclawlab.com/en/docs/automation/cron-jobs/","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0f91ee639faac77c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCheck the Gateway is running continuously (cron runs inside the Gateway process). For cron schedules: <strong>confirm timezone (--tz) vs the host timezone</strong>. OpenClaw applies exponential retry backoff for recurring jobs after consecutive errors: 30s, 1m, 5m, 15m, then 60m between retries.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0f91ee639faac77c\">>>","published":"2 weeks ago","siteName":"openclawlab.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"22689147cb371693\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nr/AI_Agents on Reddit: What's the recommended way to set up cron jobs for OpenClaw?\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNT